/**
 * App suspension (follow-up F2, Item 3): nothing SERVES a suspended app, and a
 * restart does not undo that.
 *
 *  - no route is written for an app a record holds (`handleConfigureRoute` is the
 *    only route writer), a reconfigure withdraws instead, and an unreadable store
 *    never withdraws anything;
 *  - boot makes the records true BEFORE Caddy starts: a live suspended instance
 *    (one DROP has state for, and an orphan it has none for) is deleted, every
 *    deletion is logged, and the Caddyfile on disk is never regenerated by it.
 *
 * Same faked OS boundary as platform.suspension.test.ts (FakeRuntime for PM2,
 * the bundled Postgres stubbed, the watcher a no-op, fs real under a temp
 * root). Caddy itself is stubbed at the class so "before Caddy starts" can be
 * observed: `CaddyServer.start` records what the runtime still holds.
 */
